H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_operad_skills_remaining';runpy.run_path(str(H/(P+'_synthesis09.py')));fs=json.loads((H/(P+'_preparation.json')).read_text())['files'];p=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(p.read_text())
def e(i,a,b):return {'path':fs[i]['path'],'sha256':fs[i]['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
def f(n,t,b,ev,a,v='Full body review; no retained owner invocation.',severity='medium'):return {'id':f'OPSKILL-F{n:03}','severity':severity,'title':t,'finding':b,'evidence':ev,'recommended_action':a,'validation':v}
rows=[
f(83,'Encyclopedia extraction excludes flat programme papers as overviews','The depth-only overview predicate returns true for every published/<programme>/<paper>.md, despite the discovery helper explicitly accepting flat files distinct from the programme overview. Such rows are removed before extraction. A real indexed PO001 path has exactly this shape.',[e(357,178,196),e(357,1305,1309),e(358,233,239),e(356,207,209)],'Use explicit programme identity or authoritative metadata, preserve every discovered manuscript with a disposition, and add downstream flat-programme regression coverage.','CHECK-059 evaluates the exact predicate on the scoped index path; no linked paper or generator run.','high'),
f(84,'Frontmatter parser silently discards dependency items and duplicate keys','If an inline list contains any quote, parser extracts quoted values only and drops unquoted items; duplicate keys overwrite without an error. A missing entries directory also returns an empty clean result. These can make schema consistency look stronger than the admitted source population.',[e(357,278,328),e(357,363,384)],'Reject duplicate keys, unsupported mixed syntax and missing/empty required populations; validate field types before membership/regex operations.','CHECK-060 shows a quoted valid dependency hiding a bare nonexistent dependency.'),
f(85,'Historical extraction dispositions are not bound to statement bodies','Disposition reuse keys contain kind,label,name,occurrence and match source paths, but omit statement/proof/body digests. A theorem body can change while the disposition remains. The target manifest is also read unconditionally after same-source lookup. Printed parity-gate language is not an executable proof or verification check.',[e(357,1021,1058),e(357,1096,1108),e(357,1134,1177)],'Preserve prior dispositions as history and require body/producer/evidence digests plus an explicit revalidation decision before transferring current credit.','CHECK-061 demonstrates a changed statement sharing the exact disposition key.','high'),
f(86,'Generator failures can occur after index mutation','emit_indexes and several manifest writes/prunes occur before missing declared GT sources are returned as failure. No transaction protects the generated set. --check is nonwriting but its byte-identical description is stronger than its newline-normalized text comparison.',[e(357,551,584),e(357,1234,1250),e(357,1285,1299),e(357,1354,1363)],'Perform all population/discovery validation first and stage outputs atomically with recovery; label text-normalized comparison accurately and separately check custody bytes.'),
f(87,'Type-equality checker rejects safe generated equality and accepts guard text','Frozen dataclasses already generate exact-class equality; absence of explicit __eq__ is not cross-type vulnerability. Scanner instead accepts a guard substring anywhere in unparsed source, including a docstring, without checking control flow. Dotted decorators and missing target populations are also omitted.',[e(383,40,41),e(384,17,44),e(384,49,58)],'Evaluate actual declared equality behavior or a sound restricted AST shape, recognize dataclass defaults, reject unsupported/empty scopes and retain strict cross-type negative controls.','CHECK-062/063 prove generated equality rejects cross types and the substring test accepts a constant-True method.','high'),
f(88,'Isolation and architecture PASS messages exceed their predicates','Isolation helper only ensures CWD/scratch exists, creating it if missing. Architecture discovery only includes engine* and the_symbol_game roots, excluding pfp, and never comprehensively checks inward imports. Filename/class heuristics, adapter exemptions and ignored syntax errors can pass unchecked behavior.',[e(385,12,32),e(393,42,51),e(393,159,181),e(393,225,242),e(393,327,350),e(393,375,389)],'Declare and bind scanned population, fail unavailable scopes, implement actual dependency/isolation predicates and report only the checks performed. Treat syntactic heuristics as findings, not verification.','CHECK-064 confirms root omission; helper body establishes isolation claim overreach.','high'),
f(89,'Inspector obstruction and tautology rules contain false mathematical premises','Zero d0/d1 does not force Phi1 zero: distance of omega=1 from image(d0)={0} is1. Valid exact repair on a graph needs no2-faces. A Boolean literal returned from a data-dependent match arm can compute a nonconstant predicate and is not intrinsically tautological. Universal veto rules would reject valid mechanisms.',[e(381,341,362),e(381,597,631)],'Specify actual quotient metric and admitted cell dimensions; judge dependence and falsifiability semantically. Keep real residual/source binding requirements while dropping false universal syntactic conditions.','CHECK-065/066/067 give exact zero-complex, one-edge repair and Boolean-branch controls.','high'),
f(90,'TDVP follow-on recipe omits subgradient and tangent transport conditions','The full displayed dual certificate has norm bound, saturation and tangent annihilation and is useful. However sign(Q)+P_Tperp(V) with only a norm check need not saturate Q. Contractivity of a channel alone does not imply distance to a fixed tangent is nonincreasing; a Hadamard channel sends Z in span(Z) to X outside it.',[e(369,23,41)],'Check all displayed dual conditions and feasibility; treat argmin as potentially set-valued. Transport or prove invariance of the tangent when invoking channel contraction.','CHECK-068/069 separate the valid full witness from invalid shortcuts.'),
f(91,'Normal-form CDC repair omits deterministic ties and projected dependencies','ROW_NUMBER ordering only by event_timestamp and sequence_num leaves two same-key events with different payloads unordered. The recursive BCNF sketch also needs the implied FD projection on each component, not merely original FDs whose attributes happen to fit.',[e(389,77,92)],'Admit unique immutable event ordering or refuse tied conflicting payloads. Specify projected dependency computation and distinguish finite-instance checks from all-schema semantics.','CHECK-070 exhibits two admissible tied winners; BCNF limitation is an algorithm specification obligation.'),
f(92,'Blanket Python healthy-pattern rewrites can widen strict contracts','The review rubric recommends isTrue/isFalse→truthiness and treats isinstance as an exact-type substitute elsewhere. Strict admission of True differs from admitting1 or a nonempty false string; exact numeric validation may intentionally exclude arbitrary subclasses as well as bool. Detector-zero is not behavioral equivalence or unique repair.',[e(395,56,64),e(394,41,46)],'Make semantic carrier/contract preservation a precondition of each rewrite and test wrong-type cases; keep syntax/style diagnostics separate from correctness.','CHECK-072 shows the accepted input set changes.'),
f(93,'Anti-mock snippet cannot justify its own clean-scan claim','Embedded scanner only finds ImportFrom nodes with module unittest.mock. It does not implement the advertised facade, tautology, monkeypatch, alias-import or Rust analysis, yet claims a clean scan supports their absence.',[e(371,35,65),e(371,75,78)],'Report exact predicates/language/population and implement separately tested rules before broad absence claims.'),
f(94,'Paper-reader speed and fixture metrics are presented as broad verification','Mandatory1-to-1 mapping between each claim and Python/test/notebook/Lean ignores many-to-many and noncomputational claims. Absolute1e-12 numerical agreement and finite parameter stress tests do not certify prose theorems. Report template hardcodes100 percent and sustained-and-verified language without evidence binding.',[e(361,23,46),e(361,50,75)],'Separate usability timing, mapping completeness, finite checks and formal proof. Compute each actual denominator/status and bind artifacts, premises and checker results; use relations rather than forced bijections.')]
